; --------------------------------------------------------------------- hints
hint.cw_channels = Left-click tunes a signal; F6 cycles the focus.
hint.cw_gate = Gate names the setting that is currently blocking the decoder.
hint.cw_bandwidth = Right-drag adjusts the detector width.
hint.passband = New channels are discovered only inside the search passband.
hint.no_carrier = No carrier detected.
hint.blanker = Runs before the FFT and serves the display and the decoders; the receiver blankers serve the ear only.
hint.decimation = Divides the DSP rate again; the Audio section reports the rate the path settled on.
hint.workers = Processing runs on one thread; every stage is orders below the frame budget.
hint.meter_narrow = Measures the worked band as a ratio, so the calibration above stays valid.
hint.cw_tracking = Zero holds the speed where it is; one follows every element.
hint.cw_farnsworth = Characters at speed with stretched gaps; without it every letter becomes a word.
hint.rtty_auto_invert = Reverses the polarity on suspicion and reverts if the framing did not improve.
hint.psk_rate = The symbol rate is fixed by the format, so there is nothing to set.
hint.psk_lock = Framing is the share of codes that resolved; phase is how tightly it clusters at 0 and pi.
hint.psk_afc = Read from the step between two symbols, which cannot exceed a quarter of the symbol rate.
hint.psk_print = Framing accepts any run of bits, so noise assembles codes and a few of them resolve.
hint.audio_recovered = The device came back on its own; a rising count means a cable wants replacing.
hint.rig_recovered = The link came back on its own; a rising count means a cable wants replacing.
hint.callsign_offline = Resolved from a local file: an online service fails exactly when it is needed.
hint.callsign_no_db = No cty.dat at that path, so calls are listed without a country.
hint.callsign_auto = Off lists the call alone, which costs nothing per sighting.
hint.callsign_min = Three admits the rare short calls and lets more noise through.
hint.callsign_history = A first sighting is appended, a repetition is not.
hint.spots_empty = Nothing recognized yet.
hint.spots_click = Press a frequency to tune to it; a dimmed row rests on a single sighting.
hint.decode_scroll = The wheel walks back, Ctrl multiplies the step, a click tunes to the line.
hint.layout = Sections of the selected tab, in the order they appear.
hint.layout_empty = Tab is empty; add a section below.
hint.restart = Takes effect on the next start.
hint.default_device = Follows the system default device.
hint.slider_speeds = On any slider: Shift is fine, Ctrl is coarse, both together is finest.
hint.monitor_feedback = The selected output matches the loopback capture source.
hint.monitor_band = The bar above the trace is what reaches the ear.
hint.monitor_is_receiver = The receiver chain is the listening path.
hint.monitor_needed_in_sdr = The chain runs in the monitor, so nothing is heard or filtered until listening is on.
hint.rig = The dial frequency turns the audio spectrum into a picture of a band.
hint.rig_profile = A file in the directory below, without the extension.
hint.rig_shared = Shared lets another application hold the same port through the service.
hint.rig_lines = Keep Low unless the cable keys the transmitter from one of them.
hint.rig_pitch = Used only when the transceiver cannot report its own sidetone pitch.
hint.rig_unusable = The description carries an error and cannot be used.
hint.rig_no_profiles = No descriptions found in the directory.
hint.rig_no_ports = No serial ports present.
hint.rig_click = Ctrl inverts the gesture, so both targets stay reachable.
hint.rig_entry = 14025, 14.025 or 14025000, or a band such as 40m; Enter applies it.
hint.rig_bands = A band returns to where you last were on it, in the mode you were using.
hint.rig_mark = Adds the current frequency to stations.ini, which is otherwise edited by hand.
hint.rig_offset = The control detents at zero; Shift and Ctrl together are the finest speed.
hint.rig_no_sideband = A complex signal carries the sign, so there is no sideband to choose.
hint.receiver_mode = Skimmer leaves the signal alone; Receiver filters and demodulates one.
hint.receiver_mode_link = Follow takes the mode from the rig; Drive sends this one to it.
hint.receiver_needs_iq = AM and FM need a carrier, which audio from a transceiver has not.
hint.receiver_needs_monitor = The chain runs in the monitor; switch listening on.
hint.receiver_needs_stereo = A mono input carries no quadrature channel.
hint.receiver_real_input = One channel carries no sideband to select.
hint.receiver_lower_negative = The lower sideband lives below zero here, so both edges are negative.
hint.receiver_tune = What is being received; the filter edges below are measured from it.
hint.receiver_no_tune = Demodulated audio has no tuning point: the transceiver already tuned.
hint.receiver_tune_locked = Locked: the receiver sits on the dial and a click moves the transceiver.
hint.receiver_filter = Edges are set separately; absolute on audio, measured from the tuning point on I/Q.
hint.receiver_filter_move = Shift and right-drag moves both edges together.
hint.receiver_iq = Image rejection follows how well the two paths match.
hint.receiver_iq_skimmer = The skimmer display stays single sided: the detectors are fed the channel reduction.
hint.receiver_blankers = Two blankers on two time scales.
hint.receiver_nr_method = Predictor suits keying and data; Spectral suits voice.
hint.receiver_hang = Hang holds the gain through a pause.
hint.receiver_auto_notch = Moves the notch onto the strongest steady tone; a keyed carrier is left alone.
hint.receiver_notch_two_sided = The notch runs after the detector, so it removes a tone on each side of the tuning point.
hint.decoder_off_in_sdr = Not fed in the receiver mode.
hint.band_needs_rig = A dial frequency is needed to place these.
hint.band_no_stations = Nothing listed inside the visible span.
hint.stations_click = Press a frequency to bring it to the receiver.
hint.zoom = Wheel over the display magnifies about the pointer; middle-drag pans.
hint.span_real = Audio from a transceiver fills the low end only; magnify and the view centres on what is received.
hint.anchor = Audio holds the receiver on screen; Band holds the panorama and lets the receiver travel.
hint.anchor_needs_rf_axis = Requires the RF axis: a display labelled in audio is already correct in audio.
hint.average_trace = Finds a carrier below the noise of one frame and loses anything that changes.
hint.time_axis = Age of the history, down the left edge.
hint.time_axis_needs_gutter = Requires the axis gutters, which is where the labels go.
hint.stored_view = One bookmark beside the live view, which is already kept across a restart.
hint.reference = Shift and left click on the display places the mark; the status bar then states the difference.
hint.columns = Zero takes the FFT width, below which the history is coarser than the trace.
hint.smooth = Interpolates between stored columns, which widens a narrow carrier.
hint.gpu_palette = One channel mapped in the shader; a palette or gamma change repaints the whole history.
hint.gpu_timing = Two commands per frame; the reading is diagnostic rather than operational.
hint.look_frame = The system frame is drawn in the system palette and cannot match.
hint.look_accent = Off keeps the accent for data and focus, which is what makes it mean anything.
hint.look_gutters = Reserves strips for the labels rather than drawing them over the trace.
hint.look_meter = A solid bar resolves a change a block cannot.
hint.record = The ring keeps the last recordings and discards the oldest.
hint.record_gaps = A gap is a block the disk could not take in time.
hint.record_format = 16 bit holds more range than a sound card input carries.
hint.record_block = Also the seek granularity and the dial sampling interval.
hint.record_running = Geometry applies when the recorder next starts.
hint.record_needs_audio = Nothing to record until the capture is running.
hint.replay_closed = No recording open; the display is fed from the air.
hint.replay_no_segments = Nothing recorded yet.
hint.replay_scrub = Press or drag the bar to move; the columns are the levels.
hint.replay_speed = Space plays and pauses.
hint.replay_follow = Wait at the newest block instead of stopping.
hint.export_format = Lossless keeps every sample; QOA loses the weak ones first.

